---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="About — Nrvana Studio">
  <section class="section pt-24 pb-12">
    <h1 class="font-display text-6xl font-semibold tracking-tight leading-[0.95] max-w-4xl">
      We are people who believe <em>design is for people.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg" style="color: var(--color-ink-soft);">
      Nrvana Studio is the AI design line of the Nrvana umbrella. A small, opinionated practice for individuals, small teams, and especially working digital artists who want to use AI tools well — without flattening their voice or losing their work.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section py-12">
    <div class="grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">
      <div class="md:col-span-1">
        <div class="aspect-square w-full rounded-2xl"
             style="background-color: var(--color-canvas-warm); border: 1px solid var(--color-line);"></div>
        <div class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl font-semibold">Stuart Paul</div>
        <div class="text-sm" style="color: var(--color-ink-soft);">Founder · CEO</div>
        <div class="mt-1 text-sm italic" style="color: var(--color-ink-mute);">"We make the artists harder to outwork — not easier to skip."</div>
      </div>
      <div class="md:col-span-2">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold">Why Nrvana Studio exists</h2>
        <p class="mt-4" style="color: var(--color-ink-soft);">
          Two years of "AI will replace designers / illustrators / photographers / video editors" — and a lot of "AI design" services that read like they agreed. We don't. We think the field has been pitching the wrong product to the wrong people.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4" style="color: var(--color-ink-soft);">
          Most individuals and small teams don't need AI to replace their designer. They need a working visual layer — a brand kernel, a prompt library, a tool loadout — so the work they're already producing looks like it should. And working artists don't need AI to do their job for them. They need a partner who treats their voice as the asset and AI as a tool they steer.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4" style="color: var(--color-ink-soft);">
          That's the whole pitch. We build the layer. We price transparently. We ship in days. We hand everything back.
        </p>

        <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-3xl font-semibold">What we won't do</h2>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-sm" style="color: var(--color-ink-soft);">
          <li>· Help anyone replace their designer or illustrator with AI. Hard line.</li>
          <li>· Imitate someone else's style to undercut them.</li>
          <li>· Train models on a client's artists' work without explicit consent.</li>
          <li>· Logo generators for $99. That race is to the bottom.</li>
          <li>· Volume content production divorced from voice.</li>
          <li>· Anything we wouldn't run on ourselves first.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
